-- Q72: Property Transactions: Gains/Losses [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1231, net Section 1231 gains are treated as long-term capital gains, receiving preferential tax rates. The lookback rule requires recharacterization as ordinary income to the extent of unrecaptured net 1231 losses from the prior five years, but with no prior losses the full gain qualifies for LTCG treatment.
Wrong (A): Section 1231 gains are not ordinary income when net gains exceed losses and no lookback recapture applies. Ordinary treatment occurs only when the lookback rule recharacterizes gains.
Wrong (C): Section 1231 property must be held for more than one year by definition, so qualifying gains receive long-term, not short-term, capital gain treatment.
Wrong (D): Section 1231 gains are fully taxable. There is no exclusion provision for gains on the sale of business or investment property under this section.$EXPL$
