-- Q83: C Corporations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 243, the dividends received deduction is structured in three tiers based on ownership: less than 20% receives a 50% DRD, 20–79% receives 65%, and 80%+ receives 100%. Apex''s 25% ownership qualifies for the 65% tier ($65,000 deduction), while Crest''s 85% ownership qualifies for 100% ($100,000 deduction).
Wrong (A): The tiers are set at below 20%, 20–79%, and 80%+, not as described. Apex at 25% receives 65% (not 50%), and Crest at 85% receives 100%.
Wrong (C): This reverses the tiers. Larger ownership stakes receive larger deductions to provide greater relief from multiple taxation, not smaller ones.
Wrong (D): While the tier amounts match the correct analysis, the DRD increases with ownership to reflect greater economic integration warranting more complete relief from double taxation.$EXPL$
