-- Q89: Partnerships [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 732(a)(2), in a nonliquidating distribution, a partner''s basis in distributed property cannot exceed the remaining outside basis. Cash reduces outside basis first under Section 733. Xavier''s $60,000 basis minus $45,000 cash leaves $15,000, so the property takes a $15,000 basis (not its $25,000 inside basis). Yates receives no cash, so the property retains its $25,000 carryover basis.
Wrong (A): Property does not always retain its inside basis. When cash distributions first reduce outside basis, the remaining basis may be insufficient to absorb the full inside basis.
Wrong (C): Xavier does not take a $0 basis. After the $45,000 cash reduction, $15,000 of outside basis remains and is allocated to the distributed property.
Wrong (D): While the ordering rule analysis is factually correct — cash reduces basis first, then property basis is limited to the remainder — Yates takes a $25,000 carryover basis, not the full $60,000.$EXPL$
