-- Q204: Business Law: Contracts [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the Restatement (Second) of Contracts Section 14, a minor lacks full contractual capacity, making contracts voidable at the minor''s option. Ethan may disaffirm the contract during minority or within a reasonable time after reaching the age of majority.
Wrong (A): The contract is not void. A void contract has no legal effect from inception, but a minor''s contract is valid and enforceable unless the minor chooses to disaffirm it.
Wrong (C): The contract is not fully enforceable against the minor. The law protects minors by giving them the right to avoid contractual obligations at their election.
Wrong (D): Only the minor has the power to disaffirm. The adult party (Valley Motors) is bound by the contract and cannot void it based on the other party''s minority.$EXPL$
