  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the Restatement (Third) of Agency Section 4.01, a principal may ratify an unauthorized act by the agent, thereby binding the principal as though the agent had actual authority. Ratification requires the principal to have full knowledge of material facts and to accept the entire transaction.
Wrong (A): An agent''s subjective belief in having authority does not bind the principal. Actual or apparent authority, or subsequent ratification, is required.
