  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 167(a) and Treasury Regulation Section 1.167(a)-2, land is never depreciable because it lacks a determinable useful life. Only the building portion creates a depreciable basis. Kowalski''s $200,000 building allocation produces approximately $7,273 annually over 27.5 years, while Park''s $150,000 building allocation yields approximately $5,455 annually.
