-- Q213: Property Transactions: Basis [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Treasury Regulation Section 1.168(i)-4(b), when a personal residence is converted to rental property, the depreciation basis is the lower of adjusted basis or FMV at conversion. Foster''s basis is $260,000 (FMV) rather than $300,000 (cost) because the $40,000 decline occurred during personal use, when losses are nondeductible under IRC Section 165(c).
Wrong (A): The rule does not benefit Foster. It prevents the taxpayer from recovering a personal-use loss through business depreciation deductions. No built-in loss is recognized upon conversion.
Wrong (C): Foster cannot elect to use original cost. The lower-of-cost-or-FMV rule is mandatory, not elective, when FMV is below cost at conversion.
Wrong (D): The rule does not use FMV in all cases. If FMV exceeded cost at conversion, the original cost would serve as the depreciation basis, not the higher FMV.$EXPL$
