  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 121, a single taxpayer may exclude up to $250,000 of gain from the sale of a primary residence. The ownership and use tests require owning and using the home as a primary residence for at least 2 of the 5 years before the sale. The total gain is $400,000, but only $250,000 is excluded; the remaining $150,000 is taxable.
